    "b-art-dec-h": {
      "id": "b-art-dec-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decisions"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-art-d1": {
      "id": "b-art-d1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": every agent is a vertical-slice directory under agents/<area>/<name> (areas: running, knowledge) carrying its own agent.ts, prompt.ts, context.ts, and output schema, registered in registry.ts. The kernel catalog lists them in a fixed order for the dashboard. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": scattering prompt builders across phase runtimes was rejected; keeping prompt, schema, context, and tools adjacent keeps live runs, dry runs, artifacts, and previews in step. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": apps/server/src/core/agent-catalog and every future agent."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-art-d2": {
      "id": "b-art-d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": trigger and guardian process actors are not agents; they live with the phase that owns the workflow action, not in the catalog. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": they are deterministic orchestration, not prompted work. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": apps/server/src/core/cycle-runtime/phases."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-art-d3": {
      "id": "b-art-d3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the runtime is role-neutral: prompt building and output parsing belong to the owning agent slice, and generic JSON salvage is the only parsing the runtime performs. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": role-specific branches in shared runtime code couple every agent to every other agent's changes. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime, including any future runtime helper."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-art-d4": {
      "id": "b-art-d4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": dry-run and live mode share the same prompt builders, and every rendered prompt and context packet persists as an artifact beside agent output. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a separate preview path drifts from what agents receive; that drift is a regression class this rule removes. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime/runtime and every invocation path."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-art-d5": {
      "id": "b-art-d5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": live DB-backed spawns go through the server kernel bridge with a kernel context resolver; paths that cannot inject kernel context compose the same rendered context packet into the prompt instead. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": audit artifacts, previews, and live sessions must expose the same injected input. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": apps/server/src/infrastructure/kernel/bridge, apps/server/src/infrastructure/agent-runtime/kernel-pi-runner.ts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
